## 10. Conclusion and Evaluation Limitations

The experiment implemented four recommendation strategies and generated sample outputs. Popularity-based filtering ranks frequently rated books; content-based filtering uses TF-IDF book metadata; collaborative filtering uses a sparse user-book matrix; and the hybrid approach combines content similarity with popularity.

The notebook does **not** calculate standard predictive or ranking metrics such as Precision@K, Recall@K, F1-score, MAP, NDCG or RMSE. No accuracy percentage or quantitative claim that one model outperforms another can therefore be made from these results. A future evaluation should use a held-out test set and ranking metrics such as Precision@K and Recall@K. The hybrid rating aggregation should also be checked.

